            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "I remember this one came up over in https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc/+/78891. I was never able to recreate it on our build systems and it seemed to also go away for the person who initiated the review."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Hariharan Rangasamy",
                        "email": "hariharanr@ami.com",
                        "username": "hariharanrangasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "@geissonator@yahoo.com I also faced the bitbake error after setting up a fresh Ubuntu installation. \n``` bash\nhari@msgubuntu-Dell-Pro-Max-Tower-T2-FCT2250:~$ uname -a\nLinux msgubuntu-Dell-Pro-Max-Tower-T2-FCT2250 6.17.0-1012-oem #12-Ubuntu SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Tue Feb 10 04:51:46 UTC 2026 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux\nhari@msgubuntu-Dell-Pro-Max-Tower-T2-FCT2250:~$ lsb_release -a\nNo LSB modules are available.\nDistributor ID: Ubuntu\nDescription:    Ubuntu 24.04.4 LTS\nRelease:        24.04\nCodename:       noble\nhari@msgubuntu-Dell-Pro-Max-Tower-T2-FCT2250:~$\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "AKash-A007",
                        "email": "mirrorghost007@gmail.com",
                        "username": "AKash-A007"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for the feedback, @geissonator@yahoo.com.\n\n@hariharanr@ami.com 's confirmation matches my experience exactly \u2014 this error\noccurs consistently on a fresh Ubuntu 24.04 install when building\nOpenBMC natively (outside Docker/CI). The CI build systems likely\ndon't hit this because they run inside Docker containers where the\nAppArmor restriction doesn't apply.\nThe restriction was introduced in Ubuntu 24.04 via:\n  kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns = 1\nThis is enabled by default in Ubuntu 24.04 but not in earlier LTS\nreleases, which explains why it wasn't reproducible on existing\nbuild systems. Developers setting up a fresh Ubuntu 24.04 host will\nreliably hit this without the fix.\nReference: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc/+/78891"
                }
            ],
